Prestige: Liverpool's Daniel Sturridge scores deep equalising against Chelsea
Daniel Sturridge saved Liverpool on Saturday at London's Stamford-Bridge Stadium with a hit in the 89th minute ahead of a Premier League loss against Chelsea.
Sturridge received a pass from Xherdan Shaqiri at his team's 0:1 draw at about 27 yards away from Chelsea's goal.
He aimed the ball to the left and then shot it towards the back post.
The shot sailed high across the penalty area and drifted into the top right corner of the net.
Finally, the ball fell over the jumping Kepa Arrizabalaga and then into the net.
“I was just trying to put myself in that position and getting to the ball. Players like Shaq are always playing forward as much as possible, so I’ve just tried to create as much time for myself as possible,” Sturridge told LiverpoolFC.com.
“I’ve seen Kante coming and had a contact with the ball. I didn’t think too much about it and just accepted the shot.”
Chelsea led after a hit in the 25th minute by Belgian star Eden Hazard at half-time with 1:0 remaining.
