Chelsea face the UEFA Europa League video tone at 15:00 in London on Thursday.
Tsunami death toll in Indonesia rises to 832
The death toll from the earthquake and tsunami in Indonesia has risen to 832, the disaster management agency announced on Sunday morning.
Many people are said to be trapped in the debris of buildings that had been caused to collaps by Friday's 7.5-magnitude Earthquake that had triggered up to six-metre-high waves, authorities spokesman Sutopo Purwo Nugroho reported in a press conference.
The city of Palu, which has more than 380,000 residents, was littered with the debris of collapsed buildings.
Police arrest man, 32, on suspicion of homicide after a woman was stabbed
According to the discovery of a woman's body this morning in Birkenhead, Merseyside, a murder investigation has been launched.
The 44-year-old was found at 7:55 a.m. with stabbing wounds in Grayson Mews on John Street. A 32-year-old man has been arrested on suspicion of murder.
The police urge local residents to come forward in case they've seen or heard anything.
Detective Inspector Brian O'Hagan said: "The investigation is at an early stage, but I ask everyone who has been near John Street in Birkenhead and has seen or heard something suspicious to contact us.
In addition, I ask all persons, in particular taxi drivers, who may have picked up something with a dashcam, to contact us and may have information that is of the utmost importance for our investigation.”
A police spokesman confirmed that the woman, whose body was found, lived in Birkenhead and was found in a building.
This afternoon, friends who think they know the woman arrived at the scene to inquire where she was found this morning.
Investigations are ongoing, and the police said it is in the process of informing the victim's nearest relatives.
A taxi driver, who lives in Grayson Mews, was just trying to get into his apartment, but has been informed by the police that no one is allowed to enter or leave the building.
He was speechless when he learned what had happened.
Residents are now being informed that it will take hours before they can re-enter the building.
It has been heard, as a police officer told a man that now the entire area is being treated as a crime scene.
A woman appeared in tears dissolved at the scene.
She repeats again and again, “that’s so terrible.”
At 14:00, two police vehicles were inside the barrier and another vehicle in front of the barrier.
Within the cordon stood several police officers overseeing the apartment block.
