Grieving women hang up cards to prevent suicides on bridges
Two women who have lost relatives through a suicide strive to stop others from taking their lives.
Sharon Davis and Kelley Humphreys hung up on a bridge in Wales with inspirational messages and phone numbers for counselling centres.
Davi's son Tyler was 13 years old when he started suffering from depression and was just when he committed suicide.
